==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-give up.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|<,,gave,given>}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[surrender]] {{q|someone or something}}; to [[inform]] on (someone).
#: {{syn|en|surrender|yield}}
#: {{ux|en|He was surrounded, so '''gave''' himself '''up'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''gave''' him '''up''' to the police.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[relinquish]] {{q|something}}
#: {{syn|en|forlend|q1=archaic|surrender|yield}}
#: {{cot|en|give away#Verb}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''gave up''' his seat to an old man.}}
#: {{ux|en|The king '''gave up''' land in exchange for peace.}}
#* {{RQ:Austen Emma|volume=1|chapter=7|passage="Dear Miss Woodhouse, I would not '''give up''' the pleasure and honour of being intimate with you for any thing in the world."}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} Devote or dedicate (''oneself, one's life'', etc.) to something.
#: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' myself '''up''' to working for this cause.}}
#: {{ux|en|She persuaded us to '''give up''' our time to the project.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To have someone obtain (something) to one's disadvantage; to [[concede]].
#: {{ux|en|A good pitcher will '''give up''' very few home runs.}}
#: {{ux|en|Don't tell them where you are, and try not to '''give up''' any clues either.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|author=Tyler Kepner|authorlink=Tyler Kepner|title=After Reports of Astros' Cheating, M.L.B. Is Left to Restore Trust|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230115140651/https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/14/sports/baseball/astros-cheating-stealing-signs.html|date=14 November 2019|passage=Fiers, who now pitches for the Oakland Athletics, has gone 27-12 with a no-hitter in two years since leaving the Astros. But the last time he faced them, on Sept. 9, he '''gave up''' nine runs, including five homers, and got just three outs.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[stop]] or [[quit]] {{q|an activity, etc.}}.
#: {{syn|en|cease|discontinue|blin<qq:obsolete>|[[turn away]] from (sth undesirable)}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''gave up''' the search when it got dark.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2025 October 15|author='Mystery Shopper'|title=About Anglia... and high scores|journal=RAIL|issue=1046|page=54|text=Once again, the WiFi isn't willing to work. When the guard comes to check tickets, I ask him if it ever works. He rolls his eyes and tells me it rarely does. He says I'll be lucky if I get it to connect. I '''give up''' trying.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2026-09-06|work=Skip Boring|title=Tristan Brübach, 13, Was Murdered in 1998. His Killer May Have Called Police and Later Returned to His Grave|author=Aniket Chaughule|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260908202440/https://skipboring.com/tristan-brubach-murder-frankfurt-1998/|text=A year after Tristan’s funeral, his grandma visited his grave, but she saw it had been dug up to 1.2 meters. Whoever had done it hadn’t managed to reach the boy’s coffin, and it looked like they had '''given up''' midway.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[abandon]] {{q|someone or something}}
#: {{syn|en|desert|forlet|q2=obsolete or dialect|forsake}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''gave up''' my faith years ago.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1941|month=October|title=Notes and News: Great Western Parcels Railcar|journal=Railway Magazine|page=474|text=The semi-streamlined contour of the earlier G.W.R. railcars has been '''given up''' in favour of a more utilitarian blunt-nose end, and effective floor space gained thereby.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1987|album=w:Whenever You Need Somebody|title=w:Never Gonna Give You Up|artist=w:Rick Astley|author=w:Stock Aitken Waterman|text=Never gonna '''give you up''' / Never gonna let you down / Never gonna run around and desert you}}
#* {{RQ:Rushdie Fury|page=7|passage=The optimistic peace-and-love philosophy of his youth having '''given''' him '''up''', he no longer knew how to reconcile himself to an increasingly phoney (he loathed, in this context, the otherwise excellent word “virtual”) reality.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 November 3|author=Adrian Shooter talks to Paul Clifton|title=A lifetime of railway achievements|journal=RAIL|issue=943|page=34|text="I tried retirement ten years ago. Didn't think much of it. Complete waste of time. So I '''gave it up''' after two weeks."}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[lose]] [[hope]] concerning {{q|someone or something}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''gave him up''' for dead.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[admit]] [[defeat]], [[capitulate]]; to [[desist]] for that reason.
#: {{syn|en|capitulate|give in#Verb|surrender|throw in the towel|wave the white flag}}
#: {{cot|en|give out#Verb|give way#Verb}}
#: {{ux|en|OK, I '''give up''', you win.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2007|lyricist=w:Mike Shinoda|artist=w:Linkin Park|title='''Given Up'''|passage=Wake in a sweat again / Another day's been laid to waste / In my disgrace / Stuck in my head again / Feels like I'll never leave this place / There's no escape / I'm my own worst enemy / I've '''given up''' / I'm sick of feeling / Is there nothing you can say? / Take this all away / I'm suffocating}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|finance}} To [[execute]] a [[trade]] [[on behalf of]] another [[broker]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive|US|_|dialectal}} To [[acknowledge#Verb|acknowledge]], [[recognize#Verb|recognize]] as.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=God Struck Me Dead; Religious Conversion Experiences and Autobiographies of Ex-Slaves|location=Philadelphia, P.A.; Boston, M.A.|publisher=w:Pilgrim Press|year=1969|page=45|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/godstruckmedeadr0000fisk/page/45/mode/1up|passage=The next morning, Sunday, I was boxing with R., who had come over with three or four others to swap a few with me. I was '''given up''' to be the best boxer around, and I laid them cold as fast as they came at me.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|US|slang}} To reveal (something).
#: {{ux|en|He '''gave up''' that he was the one who opened the door.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|year=2004|title=w:Paper Mario: The Thousand-Year Door|developer=Intelligent Systems|publisher=Nintendo|system=GameCube|level=Rogueport|translator=Nintendo of America|text=Well, '''give it up''', Prof! What did you find out!}}

